,87,481,220,17,18,31716,374,458,7546,30,151645,198,151644,77091,198],"messages":[{"content":"Solve the problem step by step. Give your final answer in \\boxed{...}.\n\nWhat is the sum of all integer values of $x$ such that $\\frac{67}{2x - 23}$ is an integer?","role":"user"}],"rendered_sha256":"ec5131dea9144ea0b4a009622fec57349705028a53b8d1c7b4b7672541e02f3a"},"seconds":10.69052505493164,"seed":179357661728817621,"stop":"eos","text":"To solve the problem, we need to determine the integer values of \\( x \\) such that the expression \\(\\frac{67}{2x - 23}\\) is an integer. This means that \\(2x - 23\\) must be a divisor of 67.\n\nFirst, we identify the divisors of 67. Since 67 is a prime number, its only divisors are \\(\\pm 1\\) and \\(\\pm 67\\).\n\nWe will consider each divisor and solve for \\(x\\):\n\n1. **Case 1: \\(2x - 23 = 1\\)**\n\n\\[\n2x - 23 = 1 \\implies 2x = 24 \\implies x = 12\n\\]\n\n2. **Case 2: \\(2x - 23 = -1\\)**\n\n\\[\n2x - 23 = -1 \\implies 2x = 22 \\implies x = 11\n\\]\n\n3. **Case 3: \\(2x - 23 = 67\\)**\n\n\\[\n2x - 23 = 67 \\implies 2x = 90 \\implies x = 45\n\\]\n\n4. **Case 4: \\(2x - 23 = -67\\)**\n\n\\[\n2x - 23 = -67 \\implies 2x = -44 \\implies x = -22\n\\]\n\nThe integer values of \\(x\\) that satisfy the condition are \\(12, 11, 45,\\) and \\(-22\\).\n\nNext, we find the sum of these values:\n\n\\[\n12 + 11 + 45 - 22 = 46\n\\]\n\nThus, the sum of all integer values of \\(x\\) such that \\(\\frac{67}{2x - 23}\\) is an integer is \\(\\boxed{46}\\)."},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{46}","correct":true,"format":"boxed","parseable":true},"id":"number_theory:121"}
